-V3.2 Changes over V3.1:
-- Counts native Python assert statements in AST metrics
-- Separates stable data-testid selectors from medium-risk and brittle selectors
-- Caps requirement coverage at 100 to defend against inconsistent LLM requirement counts
-
-V3.1 Changes over V3:
-- Adds three context inputs per case: requirement_summary, excutable_test_test_case (BDD), prompt (UI spec)
-- Refiner Agent now receives prompt (UI spec) for more accurate code fixes
-- consensus_agent uses assertion_score (0-100) instead of weak_assertions count to avoid double-counting
-- magic number threshold raised from >1 to >10 with HTTP status code whitelist (reduces false positives)
-- critic re-run disabled to stay within 500 RPD limit (70 cases × 6 calls = 420, 84% of budget)
-- case-level sleep reduced from 15s to 5s (~38 min total vs ~52 min)
